      "content": "hey i need some help with icd-10 hierarchy for some weird cases. we’re seeing a lot of patients with atypical pigmented skin lesions and irregular epidermal thickness that dont quite fit the standard melanoma or nevus codes. if the presentation is highly irregular or has weird textural changes, do we code based on the primary morphological feature or the underlying suspected etiology? also how do we handle cases where the discoloration pattern is non-standard?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
